    "body": "This type of confusion that you had is exactly the reason that a flat set of advances is a better API than a hybrid advance/offset combination.\r\n\r\nOriginally, transforming the data into a flat list of paint advances was required for us because it's the interface to the [text drawing routine](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/coregraphics/1586503-cgcontextshowglyphswithadvances?language=objc) we used. Now, it's no longer required because we switched to [one that accepts positions instead of advances](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/coretext/1509850-ctfontdrawglyphs?language=objc), but the argument still holds. Either way, the \"two separate flat lists\" approach doesn't require diagrams, but the hybrid advance/offset does.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
